               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate notBefore="1667" notAfter="1706">late 17th-early 18th century</origDate>
                     <note>	
                        Date based on mention of Emperor Yoḥannes, whose name sometimes has been erased and replaced with Iyāsu, fol. 3r, 31v, and throughout, Emperor Yoḥannes seems to be over an erasure as well, so the manuscript may be earlier, perhaps during the reign of Fāsiladas who is one of the few kings whose name gets erased, fol. 3r; Notes of ownership includes prayers for the souls of Emperor Yoḥannes and Empress Sabla Wengēl, fol. 6v, 31v, and throughout - but at f. 13rb,3 and f. 31,vc,6-5fb: invocation for reward in heaven for aṣe Iyasu I (1682-1706)</note>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance>Copied for ዮሐንስ, fol. 7r; Note of ownership by ኀብተ፡ ሥላሴ, fol. 1r; Note of ownership by አባ፡ ወልደ፡ ማርያም of Dabra Garizān, fol. 7r</provenance>
               </history>
